WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.034 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Welcome to the show.

00:00:01.034 --> 00:00:01.668 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Thanks. Thank you.

00:00:01.668 --> 00:00:02.869 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm so very, very happy
you're here.

00:00:02.869 --> 00:00:05.105 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Taking a chance on me.
-I'm taking a chance on you.

00:00:05.105 --> 00:00:07.674 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think this is going to work
out really well for you.

00:00:07.674 --> 00:00:09.376 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is my first American
couch.

00:00:09.376 --> 00:00:11.378 line:92%
-Oh, well, congratulations.

00:00:11.378 --> 00:00:13.313 line:92%
So I want to start with this.

00:00:13.313 --> 00:00:15.315 align:start size:94% position:6%
I did not realize
the origin of your band

00:00:15.315 --> 00:00:19.919
was that you guys actually found
each other via a classified ad?

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:22.489 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. It sounds --
its sounds old fashioned.

00:00:22.489 --> 00:00:24.090 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Like where did you get

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:26.192 align:start size:94% position:6%
your instruments,
at the Five-And-Dime?

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:28.895 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-But that was in this century.

00:00:28.895 --> 00:00:31.164 align:start size:94% position:6%
It wasn't that long ago.
-Yeah.

00:00:31.164 --> 00:00:33.033 line:92%
-Things have progressed so fast.

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:34.134 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know,
the thought of saying,

00:00:34.134 --> 00:00:36.870
"I'm going to be in a rock band"
and sitting down at a diner

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:38.438 align:start size:94% position:6%
with the classifieds seems --
-Yeah.

00:00:38.438 --> 00:00:39.472 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You're right,
like 100 years ago.

00:00:39.472 --> 00:00:42.842
-There were these two magazines,
free weekly magazines in Vegas,

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:45.545
and they had at the back of them
at each one there was

00:00:45.545 --> 00:00:49.082
a classified section, and I
would kind of scour through.

00:00:49.082 --> 00:00:50.183 size:81% position:41% line:92%
At the end of each ad,

00:00:50.183 --> 00:00:52.452 align:start size:94% position:6%
they would put what
influences you had.

00:00:52.452 --> 00:00:54.587 size:84% position:42%
And, so, I would just
look at the band names,

00:00:54.587 --> 00:00:55.321 size:84% position:42% line:92%
look at the band names.

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:56.322 align:start size:94% position:6%
And there were a lot
of new metal

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:58.558
and a lot of stuff that I wasn't
really affiliated with.

00:00:58.558 --> 00:01:00.794 align:start size:94% position:6%
At least I didn't affiliate
myself with.

00:01:00.794 --> 00:01:03.863 line:92%
And then I saw the Beatles

00:01:03.863 --> 00:01:06.533 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I saw Smashing Pumpkins
and Oasis.

00:01:06.533 --> 00:01:08.668 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I thought,
"That's close enough for me."

00:01:08.668 --> 00:01:09.936 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And that was how I met

00:01:09.936 --> 00:01:11.204 align:start size:94% position:6%
our guitar player, yeah,
Dave Keuning.

00:01:11.204 --> 00:01:12.338 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's fantastic.
And I will say, like,

00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:16.576
there's something really bold
about having a classified ad

00:01:16.576 --> 00:01:19.446
for a band which is so great
that he did it and saying,

00:01:19.446 --> 00:01:21.014 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I'm going to put Beatles
in there."

00:01:21.014 --> 00:01:22.015 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.015 --> 00:01:24.217 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know?
-It's an obvious one, I guess.

00:01:24.217 --> 00:01:26.686 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So you guys --
What was your first show like?

00:01:26.686 --> 00:01:28.088 align:start size:94% position:6%
How many people
did you play for?

00:01:28.088 --> 00:01:30.190 size:84% position:42%
Did you feel like it
was working right away?

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:32.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No. I mean, it wasn't.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:32.325 --> 00:01:34.694 align:start size:94% position:6%
We played an open mic night
at a café

00:01:34.694 --> 00:01:36.996
that was across the street from
UNLV, the college.

00:01:36.996 --> 00:01:39.999 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we just took -- you know,
we had our slot,

00:01:39.999 --> 00:01:41.167 line:92%
and we played three songs.

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:44.370 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was -- I say this
and people don't --

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:45.472 align:start size:94% position:6%
you might think I'm just
making it up.

00:01:45.472 --> 00:01:48.842 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I was looking for a spot
on the floor to throw up.

00:01:48.842 --> 00:01:49.375 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:51.811
I just didn't think I was
going to make it through.

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:54.047 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was just totally open
after that gig

00:01:54.047 --> 00:01:55.281 line:92%
to having another singer.

00:01:55.281 --> 00:01:58.184 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then it just ended up,
you know, by default,

00:01:58.184 --> 00:02:01.387
I became the singer. Yeah.
-That is -- it's very funny

00:02:01.387 --> 00:02:04.257 align:start size:94% position:6%
to think of The Killers
as a café band.

00:02:04.257 --> 00:02:04.791 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:04.791 --> 00:02:07.827
And then -- do you remember
what your three songs were?

00:02:07.827 --> 00:02:09.028 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, what did you do?
-Yeah.

00:02:09.028 --> 00:02:11.397 align:start size:94% position:6%
We did a cover of --
from a band called Travis

00:02:11.397 --> 00:02:12.465 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we were into.
-Sure.

00:02:12.465 --> 00:02:14.367 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was called "Side,"
a great song.

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:15.435 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Mm-hmm.
-And "Under the Gun"

00:02:15.435 --> 00:02:17.737 size:84% position:42%
and "Mr. Brightside."
-Now that's crazy to me

00:02:17.737 --> 00:02:20.773 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you had "Mr. Brightside"
for your first show.

00:02:20.773 --> 00:02:21.808 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:02:21.808 --> 00:02:24.444 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That seems like really
a very good song

00:02:24.444 --> 00:02:26.279 align:start size:94% position:6%
for your very first show.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.279 --> 00:02:28.314 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I had never --
I had never heard it with

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:29.516 size:78% position:39% line:92%
a beat at that point.

00:02:29.516 --> 00:02:32.752 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that was --
-You had written it --

00:02:32.752 --> 00:02:34.721 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We didn't have a drummer yet.
-Okay, I got you.

00:02:34.721 --> 00:02:38.591
-And, so, I still remember
playing it at a drummer's house.

00:02:38.591 --> 00:02:40.226
We went to his house and he had
the drums set up

00:02:40.226 --> 00:02:42.262 align:start size:94% position:6%
in his living room
and I was on bass

00:02:42.262 --> 00:02:44.764 size:88% position:44%
and Dave was on guitar
and I remember the hairs

00:02:44.764 --> 00:02:45.632 size:81% position:41% line:92%
on my arm standing up.

00:02:45.632 --> 00:02:48.501
It was the first time I'd heard
it, you know, with a beat.

00:02:48.501 --> 00:02:50.203 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was
an incredible moment for me.

00:02:50.203 --> 00:02:53.373
And I didn't know it was going
to grow into what it's become

00:02:53.373 --> 00:02:54.807 align:start size:94% position:6%
since, but I knew
that it was good.

00:02:54.807 --> 00:02:57.544
-Was it -- you say you never
heard it with a beat before.

00:02:57.544 --> 00:03:00.980
Did you -- do you also get
nervous when you meet a drummer

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:03.750
and he hasn't heard the song yet
either when you're like,

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:05.852 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Hey, I need you to play
the drums for this."

00:03:05.852 --> 00:03:07.787 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is that -- within, like,
other musicians,

00:03:07.787 --> 00:03:09.822 align:start size:94% position:6%
do you feel the nerves
of them something?

00:03:09.822 --> 00:03:10.523 line:92%
-You know, it's exciting.

00:03:10.523 --> 00:03:13.459
You never know what you're going
to get or if you're going to see

00:03:13.459 --> 00:03:14.260 line:92%
eye to eye with everybody.

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:16.262 align:start size:94% position:6%
But we've been lucky and we've
had a few moments

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:18.331 align:start size:94% position:6%
where we've tapped
into the universe,

00:03:18.331 --> 00:03:19.465 line:92%
and it has just been exciting.

00:03:19.465 --> 00:03:22.235 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You, obviously by the art
on your box set.

00:03:22.235 --> 00:03:24.637
You guys care very deeply
about your Vegas roots.

00:03:24.637 --> 00:03:25.205 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.205 --> 00:03:27.006 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's no doubt about
where you're from.

00:03:27.006 --> 00:03:30.443 align:start size:94% position:6%
Would you have said that
what your sound was

00:03:30.443 --> 00:03:31.711 align:start size:94% position:6%
was a Vegas sound?
-It is.

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:33.746
You know, we take all these
influences that you've had

00:03:33.746 --> 00:03:36.249 align:start size:94% position:6%
over your life.
You can't help but take it in.

00:03:36.249 --> 00:03:39.586 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then we funnel it through
the strip, I think.

00:03:39.586 --> 00:03:41.421 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think that's
what we sound like.

00:03:41.421 --> 00:03:42.522
-Uh-huh.
-Especially on our first record.

00:03:42.522 --> 00:03:45.825 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think you take a lot
of these British influences,

00:03:45.825 --> 00:03:47.994 line:92%
and then there's this shimmer

00:03:47.994 --> 00:03:50.630 align:start size:94% position:6%
and pizzazz to them
that those guys

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:52.765 size:81% position:41%
weren't quite bringing
from across the pond.

00:03:52.765 --> 00:03:54.067 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Chuckles ] Yeah,
and then did you --

00:03:54.067 --> 00:03:57.470
Was Vegas, did they embrace you
early on in your...?

00:03:57.470 --> 00:03:58.771 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No.
-No?

00:03:58.771 --> 00:03:59.405 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:59.405 --> 00:04:01.140 align:start size:94% position:6%
What do you think
their hesitation was

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:02.442 align:start size:94% position:6%
as far as owning you
as a Vegas band?

00:04:02.442 --> 00:04:05.411 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We wore makeup and --
a lot of makeup was happening.

00:04:05.411 --> 00:04:05.945 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Okay, good.

00:04:05.945 --> 00:04:07.113 align:start size:94% position:6%
- I was really into
the New York Dolls.

00:04:07.113 --> 00:04:09.315 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, okay, there you go.
-A great New York band.

00:04:09.315 --> 00:04:10.550 line:92%
And so I gave that a shot.

00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:11.884 line:92%
So we would go to Walgreens

00:04:11.884 --> 00:04:15.955 align:start size:94% position:6%
and pick up eyeliner
and eye shadow and lip gloss

00:04:15.955 --> 00:04:17.757 align:start size:94% position:6%
and stuff like that on the way
to the bars

00:04:17.757 --> 00:04:19.993 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we were playing at.
-That's -- I mean, they do --

00:04:19.993 --> 00:04:22.528 align:start size:94% position:6%
Walgreens, always,
they do it best. Yeah?

00:04:22.528 --> 00:04:23.429 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:23.429 --> 00:04:25.832 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I did not look great in it.
-Yeah.

00:04:25.832 --> 00:04:27.133 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I wasn't good at it.
-Yeah.

00:04:27.133 --> 00:04:31.838
I mean, I think everybody
comes from Vegas has, you know,

00:04:31.838 --> 00:04:33.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
more than --
if you grow up in the suburbs,

00:04:33.339 --> 00:04:36.042 align:start size:94% position:6%
there are so many interesting
jobs for young people.

00:04:36.042 --> 00:04:38.344 size:84% position:42% line:92%
You cleaned golf clubs?

00:04:38.344 --> 00:04:39.879 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I scrubbed clubs.
-Scrubbed clubs?

00:04:39.879 --> 00:04:41.581 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-You were a club scrubber.

00:04:41.581 --> 00:04:42.548 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-Yeah. Scrubbin' clubs.

00:04:42.548 --> 00:04:46.119 size:84% position:42%
-That doesn't seem like
one of the better jobs

00:04:46.119 --> 00:04:47.120 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
at a golf course.

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:48.154 line:92%
-No, I mean, there were caddies,

00:04:48.154 --> 00:04:50.923
and then there are the pros
in the pro shop that were, like,

00:04:50.923 --> 00:04:52.592 align:start size:94% position:6%
selling, you know,
khakis and things like.

00:04:52.592 --> 00:04:55.295 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I would -- I would wait
for the guys to finish

00:04:55.295 --> 00:04:58.398
and we'd clean their clubs
and then clean the golf cart

00:04:58.398 --> 00:04:59.299 size:88% position:44% line:92%
when they were finished.

00:04:59.299 --> 00:05:00.066 line:92%
And it was just all about --

00:05:00.066 --> 00:05:01.834 size:75% position:38%
I kinda grew to love
these kind of jobs.

00:05:01.834 --> 00:05:05.938
Hustle and bustle and you'd feel
your pocket filling, you know,

00:05:05.938 --> 00:05:06.906 size:78% position:39% line:92%
filling up with cash.

00:05:06.906 --> 00:05:09.375 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I sort of thrived on it.
-Yeah.

00:05:09.375 --> 00:05:11.611 align:start size:94% position:6%
And was there a moment
where you realized,

00:05:11.611 --> 00:05:12.345 size:78% position:39% line:92%
"Okay, you know what?

00:05:12.345 --> 00:05:14.480 size:81% position:41%
I'm going to try music
and leave all this."

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:16.749 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I met a guy at the first golf
course we worked at.

00:05:16.749 --> 00:05:18.418 align:start size:94% position:6%
His name was Trevor.
He was eccentric,

00:05:18.418 --> 00:05:19.552 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he was from Olympia,
Washington.

00:05:19.552 --> 00:05:23.790
And he had the audacity to think
that he could make short films

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:27.126
and start a band and I had never
thought of that before.

00:05:27.126 --> 00:05:30.263 size:88% position:44%
And so it just opened up
a whole new world to me.

00:05:30.263 --> 00:05:32.065 line:92%
I mean, I owe a lot to him.

00:05:32.065 --> 00:05:33.199 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do you --
-I can't find him.

00:05:33.199 --> 00:05:34.701 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You can't find him?
[ Laughter ]

00:05:34.701 --> 00:05:36.602 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The last I heard,
he was in China.

00:05:36.602 --> 00:05:38.871 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, wow.
-And I can't --

00:05:38.871 --> 00:05:41.174 align:start size:94% position:6%
Trevor, if you're out there,
man.

00:05:41.174 --> 00:05:41.708 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:41.708 --> 00:05:43.609 align:start size:94% position:6%
I love him.
I owe so much to him.

00:05:43.609 --> 00:05:47.113 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's great.
I hope we air in China.

00:05:47.113 --> 00:05:49.082 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

